WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.350 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  joyous scenes like this have been all  too rare in afghanistan recently after  two and a half weeks of competition it  was the spingar tigers who came out on  top in the spagiza cricket league  the tournament was scrapped last year in  the wake of the u.s withdrawal from the  country but while women's cricket  remains suspended the taliban has  allowed the men's game to start up again  qriket is happiness here most afghans  who face lots of challenges still come  to motivate the players  back in july midway through the  tournament there was an explosion during  one of the games in kabul injuring four  spectators  the game was able to be completed but it  was a stark reminder of the dangers that  afghans face on a daily basis  i want to tell those who oppose this  tournament that you can't break afghans  we are all one and when those people see  this crowd it's a big slap to their face  and show the unity of all afghans  over the past two decades sports  particularly cricket have been the rare  consistently positive stories to come  out of afghanistan  the men's national team set to tour  island this month both several players  considered among the world's best  cricket is the only game in afghanistan  where we're ranked in the world's top 10  and some of our all-rounders and bowlers  are in the top three in the individual  rankings we've achieved all of this  pretty quickly in around 20 years  economic sanctions have led to a  humanitarian crisis in afghanistan which  the international rescue committee has  warned could lead to more deaths than 20  years of war  despite this thousands of people turned  out to watch 32 games of cricket a game  loved by many and bringing much needed  hope during uncertain times  david stokes al jazeera

